  "item.agesandtheart.cramped_age_survey": "Survey of Reshan",
  "item.agesandtheart.cramped_age_survey.page.1": "Guild of Maintainers\nSurvey of Reshan, for the Council\n\nSubterranean, and the algae grows thick on its still waters and keeps a fair day. The party lived well here, and the Guild had hopes of it.",
  "item.agesandtheart.cramped_age_survey.page.2": "But its caverns are fissures. They climb out of sight above and below, and nowhere are they wider than a street. A town could not be built in them, let alone a city.",
  "item.agesandtheart.cramped_age_survey.page.3": "Finding: rejected.\n\nThe fissures of Reshan are colossal, and no use to us. Housing the whole population will need colossal chambers underground: vaults so wide that a city could stand on an island in their lake.",
  "item.agesandtheart.cured_ink_cake": "Cured Ink Cake",
  "item.agesandtheart.descriptive_book": "Descriptive Book",
  "item.agesandtheart.descriptive_book.named": "%s",
  "item.agesandtheart.fine_ink_bottle": "Fine Ink Bottle",
  "item.agesandtheart.fine_ink_bucket": "Bucket of Fine Ink",
  "item.agesandtheart.fine_paper": "Fine Paper",
  "item.agesandtheart.hadalfish_lure": "Hadalfish Lure",
  "item.agesandtheart.ink_bottle": "Ink Bottle",
  "item.agesandtheart.ink_bucket": "Bucket of Ink",
  "item.agesandtheart.ink_cake": "Ink Cake",
  "item.agesandtheart.lightless_age_survey": "Survey of Gomur",
  "item.agesandtheart.lightless_age_survey.page.1": "Guild of Maintainers\nSurvey of Gomur, for the Council\n\nSubterranean, as the Council now requires: stone overhead from end to end. Its vaults are vast and its lakes wide, and the rock is sound.",
  "item.agesandtheart.lightless_age_survey.page.2": "But with no sun there is no day. Within a month the party slept when it liked and woke when it liked, and quarrelled. The lamps kept us from falling. They did not keep us together.",
  "item.agesandtheart.lightless_age_survey.page.3": "At home the cavern keeps its hours by the algae in its lake, which brightens and dims as a day would. The lakes of Gomur hold nothing of the kind.",
  "item.agesandtheart.lightless_age_survey.page.4": "Finding: rejected.\n\nA home must be written with the algae in it, and a lake for the algae to grow in. Light enough to see by is not a day.",
